{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/864339-infernal-changeling","id":864339,"title":"Infernal Changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-12T09:26:46-07:00","id":864339,"title":"Infernal Changeling","content":"I've been having trouble trying to make a feudal game for DtD on its own, and wanted to try using elements from it and the CtL splat to make it perfect. It's been really difficult, and I've lost track of how many drafts I've made for this concept alone.<br /> <br /> Any suggestions on how to spin the setting to where changelings are demon-escapees from Hell? Perhaps the Inferno IS the Hedge, with the Others being Arch Fiends and Pandemonium being &quot;Arcadia&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T11:59:44-07:00","id":864417,"title":"","content":"I'm not going to convert stuff over to Inferno or such, but it's not hard to transfer concepts over a demonic viewpoint. I suppose the main question you want to ask is how entry happens-do you go to Hell when you die? When you commit a grevious sin? Or when a demon collects on a debt? Or maybe all three?<br /> <br /> I would keep it simple from there. Arcadia is Hell, Keepers are the Archfiends, I would actually get a kick out of a version of the Hedge as Dis, this burning, ruined barrier city between reality and hell, and everything else can play out to demonic lore. Shows like the Devil's Carnival can help you get a fun syncretism between the two, but mostly it's reskinning. Even the wide variety of kiths can still work, as can seemings, with just a little bit of tweaking and a lot of love for ironic hells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T14:13:50-07:00","id":864518,"title":"","content":"How should we deal with the Court System?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T14:53:30-07:00","id":864551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/864339-infernal-changeling?p=864518#post864518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How should we deal with the Court System?</div> </div> </div> </div> My guess is that Courts in this version are an attempt at cultivating virtue in damned souls so they won't be dragged back to Hell, and maybe have a chance of reaching Heaven. You'd have more Abrahamic Courts, with Bulwarks, Rituals and festivities based on figures like warrior-saints, archangels, rabbis, djinni and so on. Let's not forget other important philosophies and religions, like Buddhism and Hinduism. On the other end, you'd have so-called Heretical Courts, which could practice anything from secular humanism to cutthroat deals with the Princes of Hell. Hobgoblins like nymphs, satyrs, spriggans and dryads would give way to fiends of bone and shadow living in villages of obsidian and viscera. There would be a lot more Contracts based on agreements with supposedly holy entities, like the Contracts Of The Cross for 1ED that you can find in the Changeling Homebrew Hub.<br /> <br /> By the way, does anyone else think that the Autumn Court might consider King Solomon as one of their patrons, even though the Key Of Solomon was attributed to him falsely?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T15:29:42-07:00","id":864574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/864339-infernal-changeling?p=864551#post864551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, does anyone else think that the Autumn Court might consider King Solomon as one of their patrons, even though the Key Of Solomon was attributed to him falsely?</div> </div> </div> </div> Why care if the tale is false or not? It is a Story, and the telling makes it powerful and True.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T15:52:57-07:00","id":864593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/864339-infernal-changeling?p=864574#post864574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Why care if the tale is false or not? It is a Story, and the telling makes it powerful and True.</div> </div> </div> </div> Agreed. That's why I said &quot;even though&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T16:53:28-07:00","id":864613,"title":"","content":"You know something? This may just be the best setting hack for bringing stories like those of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heavy_Metal_(magazine)\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Heavy Metal Magazine</b></a> to CoD.<br /> <br /> Imagine, if you will, an immense battlefield in the twilit Hedge. Standing between the Ironside and Arcadia is <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9AJsl3Jxjq8\" target=\"_blank\"><b>an army of faithful changelings armed with holy Tokens and Contracts, some trusting more in God, others more in their comrades.</b></a><br /> <br /> On the other side is a nightmarish castle built from shattered bones and ruined hopes. From its highest towers, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eb2HwmHVkDA\" target=\"_blank\"><b>one shape-shifting demon forged from the sins of each changeling takes flight, mocking them and questioning their faith</b></a>.<br /> <br /> A pair of colossal, immemorial eyes that know nothing but the desire for conquest emerges from a vortex of pure Hellfire. Bit by bit, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qsIQw_yimH8&amp;nohtml5=False\" target=\"_blank\"><b>an odious and boundless form comes into view</b></a>. Wings that eclipse the stars, claws that end civilizations, and a maw that leads to oblivion.<br /> <br /> Will the faith of the heroes be enough to lead them to victory in this darkest hour? Or will the forces of Satan lay to waste all that they stand for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T18:32:43-07:00","id":864653,"title":"","content":"Well, what if you had an &quot;Infernal Court&quot;: whose members seeks to revel, believing themselves already damned, their souls tainted by their Keepers--but dammit if they won't give 'em the finger. They believe that by draining people of sinful glamour, the vibrancy of said-glamour gradually deadens, till the Others become less and less interested in then as potential slaves (though plenty in the Court succumb to monstrous temptations by corrupting the innocent for a quick fix). The Court has affinity for the Contracts of the Inferno.<br /> <br /> Then again, what if you wanted it to be where these guys really WERE demons, but because they merged with human souls, they became capable of comprehending virtue. If a creature like that of a demon can be evil, is it possible then that such a being can be drawn onto the path of enlightenment? How can there be evil demons if there are not good ones to define the former?<br /> <br /> These anomalies are constantly tempted to give into their infernal nature, it having been all they\u2019ve ever known. They're the demons who have entered our world from the realm of the Yawning Pit, masquerading in the bodies of those with weak souls as agents of the Archfiends.<br /> <br /> Unlike a normal possession, however, the magic that is used to bind demons permanently to their vessel demands them to consume the corrupt soul. In doing so, they become\u2026 different. Even if the soul belonged to a morally bankrupt individual, a single soul holds the potential for something greater. Thus, the demon in question gains a semblance of morality, and the chance to change itself rather than be forced to remain as it has for perhaps entire eons.<br /> <br /> I dunno. What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T21:07:44-07:00","id":864693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/864339-infernal-changeling?p=864653#post864653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, what if you had an &quot;Infernal Court&quot;: whose members seeks to revel, believing themselves already damned, their souls tainted by their Keepers--but dammit if they won't give 'em the finger. They believe that by draining people of sinful glamour, the vibrancy of said-glamour gradually deadens, till the Others become less and less interested in then as potential slaves (though plenty in the Court succumb to monstrous temptations by corrupting the innocent for a quick fix). The Court has affinity for the Contracts of the Inferno.<br /> <br /> Then again, what if you wanted it to be where these guys really WERE demons, but because they merged with human souls, they became capable of comprehending virtue. If a creature like that of a demon can be evil, is it possible then that such a being can be drawn onto the path of enlightenment? How can there be evil demons if there are not good ones to define the former?<br /> <br /> These anomalies are constantly tempted to give into their infernal nature, it having been all they\u2019ve ever known. They're the demons who have entered our world from the realm of the Yawning Pit, masquerading in the bodies of those with weak souls as agents of the Archfiends.<br /> <br /> Unlike a normal possession, however, the magic that is used to bind demons permanently to their vessel demands them to consume the corrupt soul. In doing so, they become\u2026 different. Even if the soul belonged to a morally bankrupt individual, a single soul holds the potential for something greater. Thus, the demon in question gains a semblance of morality, and the chance to change itself rather than be forced to remain as it has for perhaps entire eons.<br /> <br /> I dunno. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could have something pretty close to this Infernal Court by combining the Night and Dusk Courts from 1ED. Include 2ED versions of the Contracts Of The Inferno, re-skin their Miens, come up with Mantle benefits and some Titles, describe how they contribute to the Bulwark, give them infernal role models and festivities, and you're set.<br /> <br /> If you want to have infernal beings trying to be more like the best among humans, why not use hobgoblins and Charlatan Gentry? Changelings aren't playing at being people. Their kindness and cruelty can be understood in human terms, even if they are highly eccentric and have many issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-13-2016, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T05:01:53-07:00","id":864832,"title":"","content":"Personally I think a good concept to explore for the equivalent of the Hedge would be `Purgatory`, but that's just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2286-indarkestknight","name":"indarkestknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}